Use and Share Licence 1.0

This licence covers the setup pack's own files: its rules and house notes, its
scripts (sync.py, the bootstrap scripts and the setup builder), and Zoke's own
skills in it (animation, logo-recreation, cutout, chat-archive,
local-transcribe and earshot's skill). It does not cover the third-party parts
listed at the end.

1. Use. You may install and use the setup pack on any number of computers, for
   any purpose, including paid work. Selling the setup pack itself is not
   allowed (see section 2).

2. Share. You may give copies of the setup pack to others, as long as each copy
   is whole and unchanged, keeps this licence and the copyright line above,
   and is given free of charge.

3. Your own copy. Once installed, the rules, notes and settings are yours to
   change for your own use on your own computers. You may not share changed
   copies, make new works from the setup pack, or copy any part of it into
   other tools or packs.

4. Fixes. You may fix something that does not work on your computer: a path, a
   version, an error, or a setting. To share a fix, send it to Zoke (an issue
   or a pull request on this repository), not a changed copy.

5. Credit. Every copy keeps the copyright line, this licence, and the
   "by Zoke" credits in the setup pack and its tools.

6. Your work. What you make with the setup pack is yours. It puts no credit or
   mark on it.

7. No warranty. The setup pack is provided as it is, without warranty of any
   kind. Zoke is not liable for any loss or damage that comes from using it.

8. Ending. If you break these terms, your permission to use and share the
   setup pack ends.

Third-party parts, under their own licences, not this one:

- Skills in skills/ that carry their own LICENSE file: under that licence.
  HeyGen's retired hyperframes skills and motion-graphics also carry a
  SOURCE.md that says where they come from.
- Skills the setup downloads while it installs, which are not in this
  repository: real-sfx (github.com/Clipwing/skills), HeyGen's hyperframes,
  hyperframes-cli, hyperframes-registry and media-use
  (github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes), and the optional Higgsfield skills
  (github.com/higgsfield-ai/skills). Each comes from its maker under its
  maker's terms.
- The three tools the setup can install (Folio, PulseWise and MarkRoom) come
  from github.com/Zoke-Hub/claude-tools under their own licence.
